      "title": "Report Builder: Missing or Truncated Data in Exports",
      "content_summary": "Addresses user reports of data loss, mismatches, or encoding errors within exports generated by Report Builder. This typically stems from data quality issues or duplicate processing failures.",
      "content_body": "When users report missing records or truncated files from Report Builder, first verify the source dataset's integrity to rule out underlying data quality issues. Encoding errors often indicate that special characters were not properly sanitized during export. Check the job logs for idempotency failures, where duplicate processing attempts may have corrupted the final output file. If a product defect is suspected, apply the latest patch or use the known-issue workaround of exporting in smaller batches. For confirmed data loss, execute the standard data repair script or perform manual reconciliation to align the export with the source of truth."
